# Daily push notifications: GET /api/cron/notifications with the CRON_SECRET
# bearer token, once a day at 02:30 UTC (08:00 IST).
#
# One-host image (Railway, Fly, Render, docker run): nothing to set up here.
# deploy/start-one-host.sh starts deploy/daily-cron.sh whenever CRON_SECRET is
# set. Optional: CRON_UTC_TIME=HH:MM to change the time (UTC).
#
# Docker Compose (web + ephemeris as two containers) or a plain VPS: add a host
# crontab entry instead (crontab -e), replacing HOST and CRON_SECRET:
#
#   30 2 * * * curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer CRON_SECRET" https://HOST/api/cron/notifications >/dev/null
#
# Do not also run a separate Railway cron service against the one-host image:
# the endpoint is idempotent, so it would be harmless, just redundant.
